    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty strong stance. You're saying UBI is basically a non-starter due to fiscal concerns and dependency issues, but you're framing targeted programs as the only \"evidence-based\" way forward. \n\nCould you walk me through why you think the risks of UBI—like the fiscal burden—outweigh the potential benefits of, say, reducing the administrative complexity and the \"poverty trap\" often seen in targeted systems?",
